msgid "plugins.importexport.csv.results.intro.issues"
msgstr "This is the result of importing <b>issues and articles</b>. Every row of your CSV files was processed: rows that succeeded were saved to the journal, and any that failed are listed further down together with the reason they could not be imported."

msgid "plugins.importexport.csv.results.intro.issues.dryMode"
msgstr "This is a <b>Data Validation</b> for <b>issues and articles</b> — nothing was saved to the journal. The summary below is a preview of what a real import would do: it shows which rows would be created and which would fail, along with the reason for each failure. When you are happy with the result, disable <b>Data Validation</b> and import again to apply the changes."

msgid "plugins.importexport.csv.results.intro.users"
msgstr "This is the result of importing <b>users</b>. Every row of your CSV files was processed: new emails created accounts (with password and roles); existing emails updated profile data only — password and roles were not changed. Failed rows are listed below with the reason they could not be imported."

msgid "plugins.importexport.csv.results.intro.users.dryMode"
msgstr "This is a <b>Data Validation</b> for <b>users</b> — no accounts were created or updated. The summary below is a preview of what a real import would do: which rows would be created, which would update existing users, and which would fail. When you are happy with the result, disable <b>Data Validation</b> and import again to apply the changes."

msgid "plugins.importexport.csv.results.legend"
msgstr "The counters below show the totals for this run, followed by a per-file breakdown. Each failed row is listed with its row number and the reason it failed, so you can fix it in the CSV and import again."

msgid "plugins.importexport.csv.results.invalidFilesHint"
msgstr "For every CSV that had failed rows, a downloadable copy named <b>invalid_&lt;your-file&gt;.csv</b> is generated containing only those failed rows. Click the file name shown below each error table to download it, fix the rows, and import again."

